.TH MCTL 1 2026-10-04 "mctl 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mctl \- drive Mission Control from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mctl
.I command
.RI [ subcommand ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-url
.IR URL ]
.br
.B mctl
.RI [ command ]
.B \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mctl
talks to a running Mission Control server over its HTTP API. It covers the
everyday work of the cockpit without a browser: checking status and usage,
starting and following jobs, answering permission requests, running Studio
workflows, and managing terminals.
.PP
Every command prints short human\-readable output by default. With
.B \-\-json
it prints the server's JSON response unchanged, which is the form scripts and
AI agents should read.
.PP
Mission Control must be running (start it with
.B bun run start
in the repository).
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-url " URL"
Mission Control server address. Default:
.BR $MC_URL ,
then
.BR http://127.0.0.1:7777 .
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the server JSON as one document on stdout. For
.B job follow
and
.BR "job new \-\-follow" ,
print NDJSON instead (one JSON object per line, see
.BR "JSON OUTPUT" ).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help for
.B mctl
or for one command group, for example
.BR "mctl job \-\-help" .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print
.B mctl
and its version, then exit 0. Works after any command too.
.PP
Running
.B mctl
with no arguments prints the Mission Control banner, the version and the
command list.
.B \-\-help
prints the command list without the banner, so scripts can read it.
.PP
Unknown options are a usage error.
.SH STATUS AND SETTINGS
.TP
.B mctl status
Whether Mission Control is up, usage per provider (5\-hour, weekly or monthly
window), and which engine and model play the plan, execute and review roles.
.TP
.B mctl roles
Show the engine and model for each role.
.TP
.BI "mctl roles set " "role engine" " \fR[\fB\-\-model\fR \fIM\fR]"
Assign an engine (and optionally a model) to
.IR role :
.BR plan ,
.B execute
or
.BR review .
The other two roles keep their current values.
.TP
.B mctl models
Models each engine offers.
.TP
.B mctl providers
Connected AI providers.
.TP
.B mctl connections
Built\-in and connected AI agents.
.TP
.BI "mctl connection probe " id
Ask a connected agent what it can do.
.TP
.B mctl flow\-approval
Whether flows started by an AI wait for your approval.
.TP
.BI "mctl flow\-approval set " value
Turn flow approval
.B on
or
.BR off
.RB ( true " and " false
also work).
.TP
.B mctl policy
The policy template every workflow step receives.
.SH WAITING ON YOU
.TP
.B mctl attention
Everything waiting on you: permission requests, finished or stuck jobs, runs
waiting for approval. Permission requests show the request id that
.B job permission
needs.
.TP
.BI "mctl attention dismiss " key
Dismiss one waiting item. Permission requests cannot be dismissed; answer them
with
.BR "job permission" .
.SH HISTORY
.TP
.BI "mctl history " \fR[\fB\-\-limit\fR " N\fR]"
Recent chats, jobs, terminals and sessions.
.B \-\-limit
shows only the first
.I N
items.
.TP
.B mctl outcomes \-\-chat \fIID\fR | \-\-terminal \fIID\fR [\-\-after \fIN\fR] [\-\-limit \fIN\fR]
Outcome ledger of one chat or terminal. Exactly one of
.B \-\-chat
or
.B \-\-terminal
is required.
.B \-\-after
skips the first
.I N
outcomes;
.B \-\-limit
returns at most
.IR N .
.SH JOBS AND CHATS
A job is one AI run: a chat turn, a dispatched task, or a workflow step.
.TP
.B mctl jobs \fR[\fB\-\-limit\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-chat\fR \fIID\fR]
List jobs, newest first: id, status, engine, age and the first line of the
prompt.
.B \-\-limit
keeps the newest
.IR N ;
.B \-\-chat
keeps only jobs of that chat.
.TP
.BI "mctl job new " prompt " \fR[\fIoptions\fR]"
Start a job. Pass
.B \-
as the prompt to read it from stdin.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-engine " E"
Engine to run. Default:
.BR claude .
.TP
.BI \-\-model " M"
Model id.
.TP
.BI \-\-cwd " DIR"
Repository to work in. Default: the current folder.
.TP
.BI \-\-label " L"
Job name. Default: the first line of the prompt, cut to 60 characters.
.TP
.B \-\-worktree
Run in an isolated git worktree.
.TP
.B \-\-follow
Stream the output until the job ends, then exit as
.B job follow
does.
.RE
.TP
.BI "mctl job show " id
One job with its recent activity.
.TP
.BI "mctl job log " id
The full job log as raw text.
.TP
.BI "mctl job follow " id
Stream a job until it ends. Exits 0 if the job finished, 1 if it failed or was
killed. Following an existing job starts from roughly the last 4 KB of its log.
In human mode the engine's raw output is printed as it arrives; for Claude and
Codex that is JSON event lines.
.TP
.BI "mctl job reply " "id text"
Send a follow\-up message to a job. Pass
.B \-
as the text to read it from stdin.
.TP
.BI "mctl job permission " "id decision" " \-\-request " RID
Answer a permission request.
.I decision
is
.BR allow_once ,
.B allow_always
or
.BR deny .
.B \-\-request
is required; find the id with
.BR "mctl attention" .
.TP
.BI "mctl job kill " id
Stop a running job.
.TP
.BI "mctl job land " id
Land a job's worktree changes on its branch.
.TP
.BI "mctl job reviewed " id
Mark a job as reviewed.
.TP
.BI "mctl job undo " "id toolUseId"
Undo one Edit or MultiEdit tool call of a chat turn.
.TP
.BI "mctl job rename " "id label" " \fR[\fB\-\-lock\fR]"
Rename a chat.
.B \-\-lock
stops automatic retitling. Works on chat roots only.
.TP
.BI "mctl job export " id " \fR[\fB\-\-leaf\fR \fITURN\fR]"
Export a chat as markdown.
.B \-\-leaf
picks which branch of the conversation to export.
.TP
.BI "mctl job thread " id " \fR[\fB\-\-leaf\fR \fITURN\fR]"
Messages of a job's thread.
.TP
.BI "mctl job commands " id
Slash commands the job's engine offers.
.TP
.BI "mctl job queue " id
Messages queued behind a running reply.
.TP
.BI "mctl job queue rm " "id itemId"
Remove one queued message.
.SH STUDIO WORKFLOWS AND RUNS
.TP
.B mctl workflows
Saved workflows; the default is marked with
.BR * .
.TP
.BI "mctl workflow revisions " id
Revision history of one workflow.
.TP
.B mctl runs \fR[\fB\-\-chat\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-\-terminal\fR \fIID\fR]
Workflow runs, optionally only those of one chat or terminal.
.TP
.BI "mctl run show " id
One run in full.
.TP
.BI "mctl run start " "workflowId request" " \fR[\fIoptions\fR]"
Start a workflow run. Pass
.B \-
as the request to read it from stdin.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-label " L"
Run name. Default: the first line of the request, cut to 120 characters.
.TP
.BI \-\-cwd " DIR"
Repository to work in. Default: the current folder.
.TP
.BI \-\-revision " REV"
Workflow revision. Default: latest.
.TP
.BI \-\-engine " E" "\fR, " \-\-model " M"
Engine and model override.
.TP
.BI \-\-terminal " ID" "\fR, " \-\-chat " ID"
Terminal or chat that owns the run.
.RE
.TP
.BI "mctl run stop " id
Stop a run.
.TP
.BI "mctl run retry " id
Retry a run's failed step.
.TP
.BI "mctl run pause " id
Pause a run.
.TP
.BI "mctl run resume " id
Resume a paused run.
.TP
.BI "mctl run approve " id " \fR[\fIsession options\fR]"
Approve a run waiting for you.
.TP
.BI "mctl run reject " id " \fR[\fIsession options\fR]"
Reject a run waiting for you.
.TP
.BI "mctl run changes " id " \-\-graph " FILE " \-\-reason " TEXT " \fR[\fB\-\-scope\-grew\fR] [\fIsession options\fR]"
Propose a change to a running flow.
.B \-\-graph
is a JSON file with the proposed graph.
.B \-\-scope\-grew
marks a change that widens the scope.
.TP
.BI "mctl run step " "runId nodeId" " \fR[\fIsession options\fR]"
Read a step waiting on this session.
.TP
.BI "mctl run step " "runId nodeId" " \-\-post \-\-outcome " O " \-\-summary " TEXT " \fR[\fB\-\-evidence\fR \fITEXT\fR]... [\fB\-\-output\fR \fITEXT\fR] [\fIsession options\fR]"
Report a step result.
.I O
is
.BR pass ,
.B fail
or
.BR blocked .
Repeat
.B \-\-evidence
for each piece of evidence.
.TP
.BI "mctl run remind " "runId nodeId"
Remind the session about a waiting step. The server only accepts this from the
browser, so from
.B mctl
it fails with exit status 1.
.PP
.I Session options
identify who is answering:
.BI \-\-chat " ID" ,
.BI \-\-terminal " ID"
(the chat or terminal that owns the run) and
.BI \-\-flow\-version " N"
(the whole\-number version being answered).
.SH TERMINALS
.TP
.B mctl terminals
Live terminals: id, engine, age, title and folder.
.TP
.BR "mctl terminal new " [ \fIoptions\fR ]
Open a new terminal.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-engine " E"
Engine to run. Default:
.BR claude .
.TP
.BI \-\-cwd " DIR"
Folder to open in. Default: the current folder.
.TP
.BI \-\-model " M" "\fR, " \-\-title " T"
Model id and terminal name.
.TP
.BI \-\-resume " SID"
Session id to resume.
.TP
.BI \-\-workflow " ID" "\fR, " \-\-revision " REV"
Pin a workflow (and revision) to the terminal.
.RE
.TP
.BI "mctl terminal rename " "id name"
Rename a terminal.
.TP
.BI "mctl terminal close " id
End a terminal.
.TP
.BI "mctl terminal thread " id
Transcript of a terminal session.
.TP
.BR "mctl terminal sessions " [ \-\-cwd \fI\ DIR\fR ]
Past sessions a terminal could resume in a folder. Default: the current folder.
.SH JSON OUTPUT
With
.BR \-\-json ,
each command prints exactly one JSON document: the server's response. A few
commands wrap text so the output is still JSON:
.TP
.B job log
.B {"log": "..."}
.TP
.B job export
.B {"markdown": "..."}
.TP
.B status
.B {"health": ..., "quota": ..., "roles": ...}
.PP
.B job follow
and
.B job new \-\-follow
print NDJSON: one
.B {"type":"job",...}
line, one
.B {"type":"data","data":...}
line per streamed payload, and a final
.B {"type":"end","status":"..."}
line.
.PP
Without
.BR \-\-limit ,
list commands print the server response unchanged; with it, the list is cut in
.BR mctl .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MC_URL
Server address when
.B \-\-url
is not given.
.TP
.B MC_TOKEN
API token sent as
.BR "Authorization: Bearer" .
Default: the
.B apiToken
field of
.B secrets.json
in the Mission Control config folder. Only needed for non\-local addresses;
requests to 127.0.0.1 or localhost need no token. Over a token, only the job,
Studio run and read\-only status routes are reachable.
.TP
.B MISSION_CONTROL_CONFIG_DIR
Config folder that holds
.BR secrets.json .
Default:
.BR ~/.config/mission\-control .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success. For
.BR "job follow" ,
the job finished.
.TP
.B 1
The server returned an error (its message is printed on stderr), or a followed
job failed or was killed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: unknown command or option, missing argument, invalid value.
.TP
.B 3
Mission Control is not reachable at the URL.
.SH EXAMPLES
Check that everything is up:
.PP
.RS
.B mctl status
.RE
.PP
Start a job with GLM in the current repository and watch it:
.PP
.RS
.B mctl job new """fix the login bug""" \-\-engine glm \-\-follow
.RE
.PP
Pipe a long prompt from a file:
.PP
.RS
.B mctl job new \- \-\-label refactor < prompt.md
.RE
.PP
See what is waiting, then allow a request once:
.PP
.RS
.B mctl attention
.br
.B mctl job permission 32a1609e allow_once \-\-request req_123
.RE
.PP
Start the default workflow and list its runs:
.PP
.RS
.B mctl run start default """build the export page"""
.br
.B mctl runs
.RE
.PP
From a script or AI agent, get the newest five jobs as JSON:
.PP
.RS
.B mctl jobs \-\-limit 5 \-\-json
.RE
.SH NOT COVERED
Use the browser for: revealing, rotating or writing secrets; adding or deleting
connections; workflow drafts, previews and editing; the Studio default
workflow; chat home and file pickers; job images; terminal file drops; live
event streams; attaching to a terminal interactively.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/mission\-control/secrets.json
Holds the API token used for non\-local servers.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mctl " \-\-help" ,
the "Command line" section of the Mission Control README.
